<p>{{ site.name }} is owned and operated by {{ site.legalName }}. {{ site.legalName }} does not publish a street address.</p>
<div id="contact-status" class="contact-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" tabindex="-1"></div>
<form id="contact-form" class="contact-form" method="post" action="/contact/" novalidate>
  <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
    <label for="contact-honey">Website</label>
    <input id="contact-honey" name="_honey" type="text" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" value="">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="contact-name">Name <span class="field-req">(required)</span></label>
    <input id="contact-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required maxlength="120">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="contact-email">Email <span class="field-req">(required)</span></label>
    <input id="contact-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="200" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false">
  </div>
  <div class="field">
    <label for="contact-message">Message <span class="field-req">(required)</span></label>
    <textarea id="contact-message" name="message" required maxlength="4000" rows="7"></textarea>
  </div>
  <input type="hidden" name="_captcha" value="false">
  <input type="hidden" name="_template" value="table">
  <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="AI Headline Hub contact">
  <button type="submit">Send note</button>
</form>
<p id="contact-privacy" class="contact-privacy">The message and email are used only to reply. They are sent via <a href="https://formsubmit.co/">FormSubmit.co</a> to the publisher, {{ site.legalName }}. They are not sold or shared. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
<noscript>
  <p>This form needs JavaScript. You can still <a href="{{ site.contactUrl }}">open an issue on the project repository</a>.</p>
</noscript>
<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>If a story has a factual error, include the story URL, the sentence that is wrong, and the correction. A primary source helps. Read how fixes are shown on the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> page.</p>
<h2>Other ways to write</h2>
<p><a href="{{ site.contactUrl }}">Open an issue on the project repository</a> if the form is unavailable. Report a vulnerability in this website through <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>.</p>
